{
 "section_summary": "This section begins with the end of an article assessing Japan’s wartime shortages, industrial controls, and access to resources in occupied territories. It then contains two Chungking Embassy despatches enclosing intercepted Japanese commercial messages about shipping, permits, prices, and trade across East and Southeast Asia. Between them is a Foreign Economic Administration report concluding that Hainan’s immediate economic contribution to Japan was small, while its location, ports, and military facilities were strategically important.",
